on this idea post a recruitment thread later, maybe I'll see if I can jump in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game won't materialize fully before the summer at least. But when it comes around i could give it a try.<br /> I've only ever run games face-to-face with friends of many years, so i'll admit i'm a bit unsure that i could do a good job of running a game on the internet.<br /> Still, it would be the next step to beat my internet social anxiety so I'll definitely keep it in mind.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T20:27:39-07:00","id":995046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DShomshak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/518351-ask-neall?p=526076#post526076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some years back, I ran a campaign called &quot;Scion High&quot; and it worked very well. I ran it as a teen supernatural action/soap opera, though, as seen on The CW, very much in the spirit of Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Smallville, or the Vampire Diaries. Scions in a modern high school, mixing their adventures with cars, dating, afterschool jobs, etc. The titanspawn all attended the rival high school.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak</div> </div> </div> </div>DShomshak had an amazing highschool setting campaign. It was not focused on Japan, but it would make for a great read to mine for ideas for your own campaign. Unfortunately it was on the old forums, and I cannot find a copy of it anymore. Maybe someone else saved a copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:15:27-07:00","id":995496,"title":"","content":"Class of the Titians- Canadian Cartoon featuring vocal talent from Inuyasha about modern descendants of Greek heroes at a high school run by the Greek gods.<br /> \u200bThe janitor Mr. Suez has a secret just like yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The sea looks at the stability of the mountain and sighs. The mountain watches the freedom of the sea and cries.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11634-sea-envy","name":"Sea-Envy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11634_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:16:46-07:00","id":995537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sea-Envy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995496#post995496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Class of the Titians- Canadian Cartoon featuring vocal talent from Inuyasha about modern descendants of Greek heroes at a high school run by the Greek gods.<br /> \u200bThe janitor Mr. Suez has a secret just like yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>My suspension of disbelief crumbled the moment Zeus had the humility to pose as a Janitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:47:11-07:00","id":995543,"title":"","content":"If this school doesn't have a really, really intense PE coach who's some sort of Theoi-aligned Scion, everything has gone wrong.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if they have a friendly rivalry with the Teotl leader of the sports club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T01:56:38-07:00","id":995553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995543#post995543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this school doesn't have a really, really intense PE coach who's some sort of Theoi-aligned Scion, everything has gone wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did some VERY preliminary research... Is there a dedicated God of Sports and Athleticism in Greek Myth? I mean, Apollo had Art along with Medicine and Prophecy, and I think he was considered a peerless archer... Along with Artemis...<br /> <br /> And I found Nike being mentioned as the Goddess of <b>Victory</b>, but I'm not sure that's the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:07:05-07:00","id":995555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995553#post995553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did some VERY preliminary research... Is there a dedicated God of Sports and Athleticism in Greek Myth? I mean, Apollo had Art along with Medicine and Prophecy, and I think he was considered a peerless archer... Along with Artemis...<br /> <br /> And I found Nike being mentioned as the Goddess of <b>Victory</b>, but I'm not sure that's the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I can see, though my friend Wikipedia suggests that the Olympics were performed in Zeus' honor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:33:46-07:00","id":995675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995553#post995553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did some VERY preliminary research... Is there a dedicated God of Sports and Athleticism in Greek Myth? I mean, Apollo had Art along with Medicine and Prophecy, and I think he was considered a peerless archer... Along with Artemis...<br /> <br /> And I found Nike being mentioned as the Goddess of <b>Victory</b>, but I'm not sure that's the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking Hercules is related to sports (particularly wrestling) but i'm definitely not sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd imagine Socrates as the debate team's coach tho.<br /> <br /> Also Djehuty is failing half the class because no ones grammar is good enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T11:52:05-07:00","id":995727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995553#post995553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did some VERY preliminary research... Is there a dedicated God of Sports and Athleticism in Greek Myth? I mean, Apollo had Art along with Medicine and Prophecy, and I think he was considered a peerless archer... Along with Artemis...<br /> <br /> And I found Nike being mentioned as the Goddess of <b>Victory</b>, but I'm not sure that's the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Competitive sports are very much Nike's style. One is either zero or hero, never anything in between. Hermes is also connected with sports - basically, he is the god of the palaistra (although his daughter Palaistra, a minor deity or spirit of wrestling, might be more specific, she is barely mentioned in the sources I have access to). <br /> <br /> As for heroes, it's actually easier to list those who are not in any way connected to games/contests of skill. Out of those who are, Herakles and the Dioskouroi come to mind first. The Boreads, Perseus, Theseus... whatever. One can just pick whoever. The Dioskouroi are Spartans, though, so would be especially fun.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=995675#post995675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine Socrates as the debate team's coach tho.<br /> <br /> Also Djehuty is failing half the class because no ones grammar is good enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but consider: Socrates AND Lao Tzu. Imagine how those two would play off each other.<br /> And part of me refuses to believe Djehuty has time for such frivolities as teaching scions when there are lesser beings who can, but another part finds the mental image too hilarious for words. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Bonus: Aristophanes teaches literature (Frogs: remixed, what's not to love?), while sage Narada pops in occasionally to check how the music club is doing. <br /> <br /> To get back on topic: if we're talking Japan, there has to be a cameo by Abe no Seimei, because onmyodo is cool, and of course the ancient sorcerer must look like Nomura Mansai, because who else would he look like. <br /> Appearance of Oda Nobunaga or a reincarnation: mandatory. Tengu being tengu and kitsune messing with stuff: doubly mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5530-xanthias","name":"Xanthias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T00:51:42-07:00","id":995991,"title":"","content":"I think one of Heraclea's two sons might be associated with sports or possible even youth sports and coaching","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The sea looks at the stability of the mountain and sighs. The mountain watches the freedom of the sea and cries.","edited":{"userid":11634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11634-sea-envy","user":"Sea-Envy","date":". 11-01-2016, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11634-sea-envy","name":"Sea-Envy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11634_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T02:15:24-07:00","id":996004,"title":"","content":"Typically, high school lasts four years (Freshman, Sophomore, Junior, Senior).<br /> <br /> If your story begins during their first year, that's going to be a very long origin story. I think most players would get bored playing ordinary mortals (as that's essentially what they are pre-visitation) in a school that caters to the supernatural. Before they receive their visitation, they're no better than ordinary mortals with a disposition towards their patron's favored skills and attributes. So if you've got supernatural teachers instructing them in Scion activities, the chances of them getting passing grades are incredibly slim.<br /> <br /> And the visitation doesn't have to come directly from the parent either. The gods can also uses proxies and messengers to convey it. All they have to do is inform the Scion as to their divine heritage and who their parent is for their powers to awaken. And in the case of Kane Taoka, the messenger doesn't need the God's approval to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I would recommend giving them their visitation before the end of the first year. The first semester would probably be a good introduction for the students to get accustomed to the school and how it operates, before they receive their proper visitation and then things begin to get serious during the second semester onward.<br /> <br /> That way, you can spend the next three years building up their Legend by protecting the school from supernatural threats, before they finally graduate and move on to bigger things out there in the World. Maybe give them 1 dot of Legend after each school grade, so that by the time they graduate, they're on the cusp of becoming Demigods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2016, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T05:01:11-07:00","id":996029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=996004#post996004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typically, high school lasts four years (Freshman, Sophomore, Junior, Senior).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in Japan, where Maitrecorbo wants to set the game. There, it lasts three years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:42:04-07:00","id":996064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=996004#post996004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typically, high school lasts four years (Freshman, Sophomore, Junior, Senior).<br /> <br /> If your story begins during their first year, that's going to be a very long origin story. I think most players would get bored playing ordinary mortals (as that's essentially what they are pre-visitation) in a school that caters to the supernatural. Before they receive their visitation, they're no better than ordinary mortals with a disposition towards their patron's favored skills and attributes. So if you've got supernatural teachers instructing them in Scion activities, the chances of them getting passing grades are incredibly slim.<br /> <br /> And the visitation doesn't have to come directly from the parent either. The gods can also uses proxies and messengers to convey it. All they have to do is inform the Scion as to their divine heritage and who their parent is for their powers to awaken. And in the case of Kane Taoka, the messenger doesn't need the God's approval to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I would recommend giving them their visitation before the end of the first year. The first semester would probably be a good introduction for the students to get accustomed to the school and how it operates, before they receive their proper visitation and then things begin to get serious during the second semester onward.<br /> <br /> That way, you can spend the next three years building up their Legend by protecting the school from supernatural threats, before they finally graduate and move on to bigger things out there in the World. Maybe give them 1 dot of Legend after each school grade, so that by the time they graduate, they're on the cusp of becoming Demigods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah thats been a concern of mine.<br /> <br /> So far what i was thinking of going with was, have the first year into small episodes where the characters explore and solves the mysteries of the school (like the yuki onna in the school fridge). And everytime show a clue that the Big Bad is progressively getting stronger (or at least that the problems the school is experiencing all have a common source).<br /> So i wouldnt play through all the mundane school stuff (except for the very first game to show what its like and to introduce the cast). So the first year would happen pretty fast, only really being in a game when theres a festival or when something important happens. <br /> At the end of the first year the character would figure out that the Big Bad exist and where he is and after stuff i havent yet completely figured out the Big Bad escape.<br /> This prompts the character to receive their visitations during the summer.<br /> <br /> So the second year arrives and the player are proper scions and they discover that some teachers are supernatural. They will have to go on trips in japan to stop whatever plan the Big Bad is doing all the while making sure they succeed at school and train as scions. (like you said regular mortal would have too much problem training as scions and succeeding at school at the same time so i think doing that when they're scions will be better).<br /> <br /> I didnt yet thought of anything about the third (last) year yet but i like the idea that they would be on the cusp of becoming demigods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:27:31-07:00","id":996231,"title":"","content":"Well, pre-visitation Scions are more &quot;out-of-the-ordinary&quot; mortals, no? No supernatural powers, but certainly that pulp hero &quot;magic&quot;. It is a tier of play intended to be possible to use for a whole game, much like you can stay put at hero if you want, if I'm not mistaken. It is just gonna be closer to a number of Urban Fantasy stories with mortal protagonists than the early adventures of Herakles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:47:20-07:00","id":996241,"title":"","content":"Slight point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar868_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"868\" data-vbnamecard=\"868\">danelsan</a>, but there's a difference between a Hero and a pre-Visitation Scion. A Hero is a Scion immediately <i>post</i>-Visitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:07:00-07:00","id":996254,"title":"","content":"I am thinking that if it isnt 'epic' enough i might give the characters a small scale relic each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:20:06-07:00","id":996333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994662-highschool-of-the-gods?p=996241#post996241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar868_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"868\" data-vbnamecard=\"868\">danelsan</a>, but there's a difference between a Hero and a pre-Visitation Scion. A Hero is a Scion immediately <i>post</i>-Visitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why I said pulp hero (as in hero, the term in the English language, not Hero, the Scion game terminology) and specifically said no supernatural powers. Pre-visitation Scions are heroes (again, small &quot;h&quot;, not the game term), extraordinary mortals, not ordinary mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:22:56-07:00","id":996375,"title":"","content":"Acceptable. Might be a bit of confusion to have the two side-by-side for thick-heads like myself. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}